<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bishopric of Ösel–Wiek</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1228">1228</a>–<a href="/years/1560">1560</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bishopric of Ösel–Wiek was a prince-bishopric of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a>, covering the islands of Saaremaa (Ösel) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiiumaa">Hiiumaa</a> and the Läänemaa (Wiek) region of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>. Founded in 1228 after the crusader conquest and ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haapsalu">Haapsalu</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuressaare">Kuressaare</a>, it was a member of the Livonian Confederation. In 1559 the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> sold it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, which installed Duke Magnus of Holstein.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After the Livonian Order's crushing defeat by Lithuania at Wiłkomierz in 1435, the Order, the archbishop of Riga, the bishops of Dorpat, <b>Ösel-Wiek</b> and Courland, the vassal knighthoods and the towns agreed at Walk (Valga) to settle disputes peacefully and defend one another.</blockquote><a href="/state/livonian-confederation">Livonian Confederation</a></li><li><blockquote>Terra Mariana was never a single state but a patchwork: the Archbishopric of Riga, the bishoprics of Dorpat, <b>Ösel-Wiek</b> and Courland, the Livonian Order, the Danish Duchy of Estonia (1219-1346), and powerful towns such as Riga and Reval.</blockquote><a href="/state/terra-mariana">Terra Mariana</a></li></ul></section>
